<title>GERMANY: German Oct/Nov sugar output up at 3.39 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>German Oct/Nov sugar output up at 3.39 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German domestic sugar output in the first two months of the 1996/97 (Oct/Sept) season totalled 3.39 million tonnes, rounded, compared with 3.02 million in Oct/Nov 1995, sugar industry association WVZ said on Monday.</p>
<p>Oct and Nov are the busiest months in the sugar year, with 95/96 full season sugar output at 3.83 million.</p>
<p>WVZ's monthly statistics circular said November sugar output alone was 1.54 million tonnes versus 1.47 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>Domestic sugar sales in November amounted to 233,391 tonnes compared with 241,155 in November 1995.</p>
<p>Stocks at the end of November totalled 2.75 million tonnes versus 2.41 previously.</p>
<p>November imports of 6,777 tonnes were down from 7,193 in 1995 while exports of 168,295 tonnes compared with 174,281 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>Cumulative details (in tonnes) --</p>
<p>					   Oct/Nov 1996	Oct/Nov 1995</p>
<p>    Domestic sugar output	   3,387,236	  3,021,452</p>
<p>    Imports				  16,585	     23,649</p>
<p>    Exports				 390,354	    378,149</p>
<p>    Domestic sales			506,278	    508,590</p>
<p>    Carry-in stocks on Oct 1	  239,562	    250,854</p>
<p>-- Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
